;; frames, stop, is_tracing, get_traceback_limit, clear_traces, reset_peak) and its start by PYTHONTRACEMALLOC or
;; -X tracemalloc[=N], as CPython checks them; no allocation is traced yet. pyi allocates through Go: there is no allocator
;; to hook, and no free to see but the collector's (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "Design: 220" and "As built: 220": what
;; an allocation is decided as, and the second stage). So _get_traces is [], _get_object_traceback None,
;; get_traced_memory (0, 0) and get_tracemalloc_memory 0: tracemalloc's Snapshot, Filter, Traceback and statistics work
